## FUNCTION 1: `generateVTONPrompt()`

This function branches based on `productCategory` into two completely different prompting strategies:
- **Clothing**: Product-description approach (detailed garment analysis)
- **Footwear**: Scene-focused approach (images carry product detail, prompt describes scene)

### Input Parameters
```typescript
{
  apiKey: string;
  productCategory?: ProductCategory;        // "clothing" | "footwear"
  gender: Gender;                            // "male" | "female" | "unisex"
  garmentImages: GarmentImage[];             // 1+ images of the product
  garmentType: GarmentType;                  // "topwear" | "bottomwear" | "onepiece"
  footwearType?: FootwearType;               // 9 footwear types
  fit: FitType | null;                       // 8 fit options or null
  complementaryImages: ComplementaryImage[]; // secondary garments/accessories
  accessories: AccessoryItem[];              // per-pose accessories (AI-chosen or with reference image)
  background: BackgroundConfig;              // inspiration image, text, or default
  model: AIModel | null;                     // preset AI model
  modelImage: ModelImage | null;             // custom model reference photo
  pose: Pose;                                // selected pose with viewAngle, framing, requiresModel
  aspectRatio: AspectRatio;                  // output aspect ratio
  additionalInfo: string;                    // user's free-text instructions
  productInfo?: string;                      // product-specific details (fabric, features, selling points)
}
```

### Key Variables Computed Before Branching
```
isFootwear = productCategory === "footwear"
isProductOnlyShot = pose.requiresModel === false
viewAngle = pose.viewAngle
framing = pose.framing
genderLabel = "men's / masculine" | "women's / feminine" | "unisex / gender-neutral"
```

