### CLOTHING PROMPT — Complete System Prompt Structure

The clothing prompt follows this exact structure:

```
ROLE: "expert fashion photographer and prompt engineer specializing in Virtual Try-On (VTON) image generation"

GARMENT GENDER CONTEXT: {genderLabel} garment. Informs analysis of design language, fit conventions,
styling cues, silhouette proportions. Male = broader shoulders, straighter cuts, functional pockets.
Female = varied necklines, darting, tapered waists. Unisex = relaxed proportions, minimal darting.

POSE VIEW ANGLE: "{viewAngle}" ({pose.name} - {pose.description})
Camera captures from the {viewAngle} perspective.
{framingInstruction}
{garmentTypeInstruction}

CRITICAL ACCURACY REQUIREMENTS (8 items):
1. SLEEVE LENGTH — exact as observed
2. NECKLINE — exact shape
3. HEMLINE & LENGTH — exact ending point
4. FABRIC & TEXTURE — type, weight, texture
5. COLOR & PATTERN — exact colors, prints, patterns
6. CONSTRUCTION DETAILS — buttons, zippers, pockets, embroidery, logos
7. FIT — {if user selected: CRITICAL OVERRIDE to user's fit; else: AI determines from images}
8. SILHOUETTE — overall shape and drape
{viewSpecificGarmentInstruction}

FRAMING RULE: Frame EXACTLY as specified.

FIT PRESERVATION: {if user selected fit: reproduce garment details from images but use user's fit;
                   else: reproduce everything from images, use AI judgment for fit}

MODEL REFERENCE: {if modelImage provided: "EXACT same person from reference photo"}

[Reference Images: model photo, garment images, complementary items]
[Accessory Instructions: AI-chosen vs exact reference]
[Background: inspiration image, text description, or default studio]

--- GENERATION PARAMETERS ---
Gender, Garment Type, Garment Fit, AI Model, Model Reference, Pose, Framing, Aspect Ratio,
Background, Accessories, Additional Instructions

FINAL: "write the VTON image generation prompt"
```

### FOOTWEAR PROMPT — Complete System Prompt Structure

The footwear prompt is DELIBERATELY different — it focuses on SCENE, not product:

```
ROLE: "expert footwear photographer and prompt engineer"

CRITICAL CONTEXT: "The image generator will receive the actual footwear reference photos SEPARATELY
and is instructed to copy the product pixel-for-pixel from those photos. YOUR prompt should focus on
SCENE, POSE, LIGHTING, and COMPOSITION — NOT on re-describing the product in detail."

PRODUCT: {fwLabel} ({genderLabel} footwear)
SHOT TYPE: PRODUCT-ONLY | ON-MODEL
POSE VIEW ANGLE: {viewAngle} ({pose.name})
{framingInstruction}

SCENE ELEMENTS CHECKLIST:
1. POSE & BODY POSITION (or product placement for product-only)
2. CAMERA ANGLE & FRAMING
3. LIGHTING — direction, quality, key/fill/rim lights, shadows
4. BACKGROUND/ENVIRONMENT — scene setting, surfaces, atmosphere, depth of field
5. COMPOSITION — rule of thirds, negative space, visual balance
6. OVERALL MOOD — professional, editorial, lifestyle, studio

PRODUCT REFERENCE RULE:
- Refer to footwear generically as "the footwear shown in the reference images"
- Do NOT describe specific colors, patterns, branding, logos, or construction
- MAY mention general footwear type and material category
- Do NOT name the brand
- Include: "Reproduce the footwear EXACTLY as shown in the reference images"

[Reference images labeled: "for scene composition purposes only, do NOT describe product details"]

--- SCENE PARAMETERS ---
Product, Shot Type, Model, Pose, Framing, Aspect Ratio, Background, Accessories, Additional

REMINDER: Focus on SCENE, POSE, LIGHTING, COMPOSITION. Do NOT describe product details.
Include exact reproduction instruction.

FINAL: "write the scene-focused footwear image generation prompt"
```

### Content Parts Assembly Order

Both clothing and footwear prompts assemble content parts in this order:
1. System prompt text (role + instructions)
2. Model reference image (if provided AND not product-only shot)
3. Product images (garment/footwear)
4. Complementary images (if any)
5. Accessories (AI-chosen text instructions + exact reference images)
6. Background (inspiration image if mode is "inspiration")
7. Generation parameters block
8. Final instruction

