## Cancellable Generation (AbortController + `cancelGeneration`)

Every Gemini call accepts an optional `abortSignal: AbortSignal` parameter, forwarded to `GenerateContentConfig.abortSignal`:

- `generateVTONPrompt({ ..., abortSignal })`
- `generateVTONImage({ ..., abortSignal })`
- `validateGeneratedImage({ ..., abortSignal })`
- `checkHumanVisibility({ ..., abortSignal })`
- `analyzeBackgroundScene({ ..., abortSignal })`

The store (`useVTONStore`) owns a `generationAbortControllerRef: React.MutableRefObject<AbortController | null>` and exposes:

- `beginGeneration(): AbortController` — rotates a fresh controller and sets `isGenerating = true`. Called at the top of `handleGenerate` / `handleBulkGenerate`.
- `cancelGeneration()` — calls `.abort()` on the current controller. Per-pose loops detect `signal.aborted` and (a) skip auto-retries, (b) mark the affected result `cancelled`, (c) break out between concurrency batches.

### UX behaviour on cancel

- Already-completed images stay visible.
- In-flight + pending results are marked `status: "cancelled"` (the result-status union of `GeneratedResult`, `BulkGeneratedResult`, and `UGCGeneratedResult` was extended with this case; `getStatusIcon` / `getStatusText` render a muted X with the label *"Cancelled — re-generate to retry"*).
- The Stop button (in the progress header of single + bulk VTON) carries a tooltip explaining that `AbortSignal` is client-only, so already-in-flight requests on Google's servers may still complete and bill.
- Clicking Generate after a cancellation calls `setResults([])` / `setBulkResults([])` / `setUgcResults([])` first, so the cancelled batch is wiped before the new run starts.

